    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37346" root="كوح" body-key="k">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَاحَهُ</span></b> , [aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَكُوحُ</span>,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَوْحٌ</span>; and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كوّحهُ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اكاحهُ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كاوحهُ</span></b> ; <i>He
fought with him and overcame him:</i> (K:) so
Az, explains <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كاوحهُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُكَاوَحَةٌ</span>: or, accord.
to the M, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كاوحهُ</span></b>  signifies <i>he fought with him;</i>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كاحه</span>, <i>he overcame him;</i> (TA;) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كوّحهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكْوِيحٌ</span>, also has this last signification; (IAar, S, TA;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اكاحهُ</span></b> , inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِكَاحَةٌ</span>. (IAar, TA.)

